message.content:
This looks like the AD/CVD scope on aluminum "enclosures" or a CBP ruling on an empty aluminum electrical cabinet. Candidate headings are 8537.10 (boards, cabinets with apparatus for electric control or distribution, for ≤1000V), 8538.10 (parts: boards, panels, consoles, desks, cabinets and other bases for goods of 8537, not equipped with apparatus), and 7610 or 7616 (aluminum structures).

Heading 8538.10 covers empty cabinets specifically designed for 8537 apparatus. Classification as 8538.10.00 is likely, with the statistical suffix 8538.10.0000 as the full code. The cabinet houses power distribution equipment and fiber optic equipment, which may not be only 8537 goods, so 7616.99 is possible. However, CBP rulings on empty electrical enclosures generally put them in 8538.10.0000, as "other bases for goods of heading 8537, not equipped with their apparatus."

{"hts_code": "8538.10.0000", "reason": "An empty cabinet designed to house electrical distribution/control apparatus is classified as a part of heading 8537 goods, specifically 'cabinets and other bases, not equipped with their apparatus,' under 8538.10."}
